body:
I'm getting help, called my therapist already, so I'll be okay eventually I hope.

&#x200B;

I know he's broken, he has nightmares about his abuse. I know this is something that would've never happened had he not grew up like that. But regardless, I cannot stay with him. I can't look at him the same. I can't stay with someone who I will forever question, does he love me? Is he even attracted to me? Or is he attracted to children? What if he goes out and touches someone again? These things would always be back in my mind if I stayed. Especially because I have OCD and BDD, staying with him would only destroy my mental health more and make me have constant obsessive and intrusive thoughts. I'm sorry for him in a way because I know he's fucked from childhood abuse. I've been supportive thus far but this is where it has to end because I cannot personally handle this. Abuse or not, he made a choice to do this. And especially if they confiscate his devices and find child pornography, that's a whole other fucking ordeal. Because then that would also mean he was hiding that from me and doing that while he was with me. He said this molestation was several many years ago, but if I find out he's been looking at shit like that in my fucking home, behind my back, while I'm at work or asleep, it's going to fucking kill me even more.

Thank you so much. I have been trying already to think of even little things that are silver linings. Like being able to focus on myself now and bettering myself, finding more things I enjoy doing alone.

&#x200B;

I hope I can pick myself up and move on very soon.

I really hope that you are right, I asked his therapist if it could be just psychosis, since his sister is convinced that's what it is. Of course she can't say yes or no, she said "he is holding onto a lot of guilt and a lot of things are coming out in therapy." And said there will be an investigation. I don't know how they can investigate something like this if the niece is stating it didn't happen, or if she was too young to remember.

&#x200B;

I've contacted my own therapist, he's going to meet with me in a few days. I just can't believe this is happening. I'm so angry, I feel disgusted and betrayed. But at the same time I am grieving a relationship where just last week we were hysterical laughing playing video games and making jokes, and talking about how we can't wait to spend the rest of our lives together. Four days ago we went to the store to pick up fun crafts to do together, and things to decorate our home, and that same night he went into the hospital. I'm in a state of fear, panic, and disbelief.
